{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Elimination Ideal.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Elimination Ideal.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"elimination ideal elimination ideal","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Elimination Ideal.md","fileName":"Elimination Ideal.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Elimination Ideal","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-13 19:45\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Polynomial Algorithms and Elimination]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Polynomial Algorithms and Elimination","Elimination Theorem","commutativealgebra.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Elimination Ideal.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Elimination Ideal.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"elimination ideal elimination ideal","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Elimination Ideal.md","fileName":"Elimination Ideal.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Elimination Ideal","heading":"Elimination Ideal","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"For an ideal I in K[x₁,…,xₙ], the ℓ-th elimination ideal is I ∩ K[xₗ₊₁,…,xₙ]. It contains exactly the consequences of I that do not involve the first ℓ variables.\n\nComputing a Gröbner basis in lexicographic order exposes this intersection through the [[Elimination Theorem]]. Elimination ideals describe projections and produce implicit equations from parametrizations.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Polynomial Algorithms and Elimination","Elimination Theorem","commutativealgebra.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Elimination Ideal.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Elimination Ideal.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"elimination ideal elimination ideal","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Elimination Ideal.md","fileName":"Elimination Ideal.md","folder":"6 - F